<div id="listbox-button-overview">
    <h1>Listbox Button Component</h1>
    
    <p>
        A listbox button is intended for use as a custom implementation of the native HTML select element's${" "}
        <em>single</em>
         -select use case.
    </p>
    <p>
        Because a button element does not store form data, its value will not be submitted along with other form data without the assistance of JavaScript.
    </p>
    
    <h2>Terminology</h2>
    <p>We use the following terminology when discussing this pattern.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>widget</strong>: the pattern as a whole, comprised of the parts below
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>button</strong>: the button that opens the flyout
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>popover</strong>: the overlay element that contains the listbox
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>listbox</strong>: the list of options
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>option</strong>: an option, with state
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>label</strong>: internal and/or external text element(s)
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>
